<%# DATA-LAYER HEALTH BANNER (#3) -- the kb's `.banner.warn` under the header,
    backported. ONE line, amber, listing the audit's unresolved checks and
    linking to /audit for the full picture.

    FED BY THE AUDIT, NOT A SECOND IMPLEMENTATION: `AuditGaps.banner` is a
    projection of `AuditGaps.report` -- the SAME document /audit renders -- so
    the banner and the page cannot disagree about what is wrong.

    Rendered by the LAYOUT, under the header, on every authed page. It renders
    NOTHING when the data layer is clean: a banner that is always there is
    chrome, not a warning. %>
<% gaps = AuditGaps.banner %>
<% if gaps.any? %>
  <div class="banner warn" role="status" data-health-banner>
    <div class="container">
      <span class="banner-label">data debt:</span>
      <span class="banner-list"><%= gaps.map { |name, n| "#{name} (#{n})" }.join(" · ") %></span>
      <a href="<%= audit_path %>" class="banner-link">full audit →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
<% end %>
